\draw[thick,<->,domain=-4.2:1.45,smooth,samples=80,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(\x*ln(3))});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph of $y = x^2$ is drawn for the domain $x \geq 1$.
What is its range?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.45]
\draw[gray!25,very thin] (-1,-1) grid (4,9);
\draw[->] (-1.3,0)--(4.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.3)--(0,9.3) node[above] {$y$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,-0.12) {$1$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,-0.12) {$2$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-0.12) {$3$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,2) {$2$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,4) {$4$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,6) {$6$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,8) {$8$};
\draw[thick,->,domain=1:3,smooth,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (3pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

